detect the SDB using at least one of: (iii) the fusion signals, (iv) the second signals, or (v) the acoustic signals; and

determine a responsive action to detection of the SDB.



44.    (New) The system of claim 43, wherein the processor is further configured to determine an intensity, magnitude, duration, and type of the SDB.



45.    (New) The system of claim 43, wherein the responsive action is one or more of:

an audible tone;

an audible message;

a trigger for a home automation device;

a trigger for a speech assistant device;

a call to an entity or emergency services;

marking data for future access;

a database entry; and

a health check.



46.    (New) A device comprising:

a substrate configured to support a subject;

a plurality of non-contact sensors configured to capture signals with respect to the subject;

a processor in connection with the plurality of sensors, the processor configured to:determine biosignals from the signals to monitor a health status of the subject;

detect presence of speech in an acoustic signal; and

detect a verbal command in the speech, wherein, in response to not detecting presence of the verbal command, the processor is configured to perform a sleep disordered breathing (SDB) analysis.
